course: dictionary
lesson: 14359
title: Onshore and offshore
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Onshore means on the land, not at sea. Shore is the edge where the land meets the sea, and on tells you the land is where the thing is. «The wind farm was built onshore, on the hills above the town.» The clue is the hills above the town: the turbines are on the land.
explain: The same word can describe wind. «The onshore breeze blew the smell of salt up the beach.» Here onshore means the wind is blowing from the sea towards the land. Ask yourself: which way is the wind moving? If it comes off the water and blows in towards you on the beach, it is onshore.
explain: Onshore can also describe money and business. «The company kept all its jobs onshore, inside the country.» Here onshore means inside your own country rather than abroad. The clue is that the work stays at home and is not sent overseas.
fact: Onshore means on the land, not at sea.
fact: An onshore wind blows from the sea towards the land.
fact: Onshore wind turbines are built on land, often on hills.
fact: Offshore is the opposite idea: offshore wind turbines are built out at sea.
fact: For money and business, onshore means inside a country rather than abroad.
exercise: «The wind farm was built onshore, on the hills above the town.» Where was the wind farm built? | *On the land | In another country | Under the ground | Out at sea
exercise: «The onshore breeze blew the smell of salt up the beach.» Which way was the wind blowing? | From the land out to sea | It was not blowing at all | *From the sea towards the land | Straight up into the sky
exercise: «The company kept all its jobs onshore.» What does onshore mean here? | Under the water | *Inside the country | Abroad, in another country | Out at sea
test: Surfers said, «The onshore wind made the waves messy.» What did the onshore wind do to the waves? | *Made them messy | Turned them into ice | Stopped them completely | Made them flat and calm
test: A wind farm of turbines on a hill, far from the sea, is called what kind of wind farm? | Underwater | *Onshore | Ocean-going | Offshore
exam: «The company wanted its goods made onshore, not abroad.» What does onshore mean here? | In the sky | *Inside the country | Out at sea | Very cheap
